---
const faqs = [
    {
        q: "What is Zoo, exactly?",
        a: "A self-hosted service that gives AI agents disposable computers: Linux, macOS and Windows desktops, browsers and code shells, each in its own microVM with its own kernel. Agents drive them over MCP, REST or an SDK; you watch and take over from the dashboard.",
    },
    {
        q: "What do I need to run it?",
        a: "A Debian or Ubuntu server with KVM (bare metal, or a cloud VM with nested virtualization), or macOS / Windows with Docker Desktop running. macOS sandboxes need Apple Silicon; Windows sandboxes need Hyper-V.",
    },
    {
        q: "How do agents connect?",
        a: "One MCP server at /mcp/ with an API key, plain REST endpoints, or the Python and TypeScript SDKs. Every tool is registered once and exposed identically over all of them, so switching is cheap.",
    },
    {
        q: "Can I watch what agents are doing?",
        a: "Yes. Live view streams a sandbox's screen in the browser with mouse and keyboard control, and tool calls land in the activity log.",
    },
    {
        q: "Where does my data live?",
        a: "On your servers. Sandboxes, dashboard, database and secrets all run on your hardware. Secrets are encrypted at rest, with optional AWS, Google Cloud or Vault KMS.",
    },
    {
        q: "Does it work with Claude Code?",
        a: "Code sandboxes ship with Claude Code installed. Supply your own credentials as an encrypted secret and run it through the sandbox's shell tools. Zoo does not supply a model or a planner.",
    },
    {
        q: "Can it run on more than one server?",
        a: "Yes. Kubernetes distributes Linux sandboxes across nodes, and Mac and Windows hosts join as remote servers for native guests.",
    },
];
---

<section class="zsection" id="faq">
    <div class="container narrow">
        <header class="zhead" data-reveal>
            <span class="kicker">ⓘ visitor information</span>
            <h2>Questions, answered plainly</h2>
        </header>

        <div class="faq" data-reveal>
            {
                faqs.map((f, i) => (
                    <details open={i === 0}>
                        <summary>
                            <span>{f.q}</span>
                            <span class="plus pixel" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        </summary>
                        <p>{f.a}</p>
                    </details>
                ))
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    .narrow {
        max-width: 820px;
    }

    .faq {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.7rem;
    }

    details {
        background: var(--paper);
        border: 2px solid var(--ink);
        border-radius: 12px;
        transition: box-shadow 0.2s, transform 0.2s;
    }

    details[open] {
        box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 var(--ink);
        transform: translate(-2px, -2px);
    }

    summary {
        display: flex;
        justify-content: space-between;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 1rem;
        padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
        cursor: pointer;
        list-style: none;
        font-size: 1.08rem;
        font-weight: 560;
    }

    summary::-webkit-details-marker {
        display: none;
    }

    .plus {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        width: 28px;
        height: 28px;
        flex: none;
        background: var(--yellow);
        border: 2px solid var(--ink);
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1;
        transition: background 0.2s, color 0.2s;
    }

    .plus::before {
        content: "+";
    }

    details[open] .plus::before {
        content: "−";
    }

    details[open] .plus {
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--yellow);
    }

    details p {
        padding: 0 1.2rem 1.15rem;
        color: var(--ink-2);
        max-width: 66ch;
    }
</style>
